<section image-layout="blank" id="0Mdse-4tmE" vertical-align="center"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item><p role="eyebrow">A teaching heuristic—not a universal formula</p><h2>Dialectic follows a position until its own promise comes under pressure</h2><p font-size="18pt">The movement is not a mechanical thesis–antithesis–synthesis sequence. A determinate position is specified, worked through, and revised when its own commitments reveal a limitation.</p><freeform-block w="840" h="220"><box type="content" x="0" y="0" w="560" h="220" sizing="fixed" background-color="surface" style="border: 1pt solid var(--neutral-border-color); border-radius: 4pt;"></box><box type="content" x="24" y="16" w="500" h="30" sizing="fixed"><p role="eyebrow">Inside one determinate position</p></box><box type="content" x="28" y="62" w="205" h="130" sizing="fixed" vertical-align="center"><p role="eyebrow">What it claims</p><h3>Removing limits increases freedom.</h3></box><shape preset="rightArrow" x="238" y="105" w="58" h="24" fill="accent" stroke-width="0"></shape><box type="content" x="302" y="62" w="226" h="130" sizing="fixed" vertical-align="center"><p role="eyebrow">What follows</p><h3>The practice can silence the voices it promised to free.</h3></box><shape preset="rightArrow" x="574" y="99" w="54" h="30" fill="palette-3" stroke-width="0"></shape><box type="content" x="640" y="36" w="200" h="150" sizing="fixed" vertical-align="center" background-color="palette-2" style="padding: 14pt 16pt; border-radius: 4pt;"><p role="eyebrow">Richer account</p><h3>Freedom needs enabling relations, not only absent limits.</h3></box></freeform-block><p font-size="18pt"><b>The pressure is internal:</b> the consequence is assessed against the position’s own promise.</p><p role="caption">Source: <a href="https://plato.stanford.edu/entries/hegel-dialectics/">Stanford Encyclopedia of Philosophy, “Hegel’s Dialectics”</a></p></grid-item></grid></section>